Summary: Stop WMI queries deadlocking on wbemprox's per-table lock (backport from Wine 10.5)
Category: system
Kind: fix
Origin: winehq
  Commit: b93bee1a8748c178a5acb0b220de6f7d62ad807d
  URL: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/commit/b93bee1a8748c178a5acb0b220de6f7d62ad807d
  Note: upstream commit b93bee1a8748c178a5acb0b220de6f7d62ad807d (Hans Leidekker)
Upstream: yes, in Wine 10.5 (Wine bug 56859)
Why: On 10.0, Big Fish trial games' WMI queries hang on "dlls\wbemprox\builtin.c: table.cs"; RtlpWaitForCriticalSection logs 60-second timeouts until it recovers.
Programs: Big Fish trial games (White Wolf, Waverly Academy, Deadly Device):
 WMI queries hang on wbemprox's table lock (60-second timeouts) on 10.0
Evidence: second-chance-78's Big Fish trials (White Wolf, Waverly Academy) on macfixes-10.0-build4 logged six such timeouts.
Port: Upstream's patch, unchanged; it applies to 10.0 with only a line offset in builtin.c. Five of the six files it touches are identical in 10.0 and in its upstream parent (50b1a253d6). builtin.c differs only in code unrelated to the tables' lock.
Status: built in macfixes-10.0-build5. 2026-11-16: no table.cs timeouts in
 10 Big Fish trial launches (White Wolf, Waverly Academy, Deadly Device), all passing.

diff --git a/dlls/wbemprox/builtin.c b/dlls/wbemprox/builtin.c
index a3f0d9afcce..2e3c3ce041e 100644
--- a/dlls/wbemprox/builtin.c
+++ b/dlls/wbemprox/builtin.c
@@ -4635,13 +4635,27 @@ void init_table_list( void )
     {
         list_init( &tables[ns] );
         for (i = 0; i < builtin_namespaces[ns].table_count; i++)
+            list_add_tail( &tables[ns], &builtin_namespaces[ns].tables[i].entry );
+        table_list[ns] = &tables[ns];
+    }
+}
+
+void free_dynamic_tables( void )
+{
+    UINT ns;
+
+    for (ns = 0; ns < ARRAY_SIZE(builtin_namespaces); ns++)
+    {
+        struct table *table, *next;
+
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY_SAFE( table, next, table_list[ns], struct table, entry )
         {
-            struct table *table = &builtin_namespaces[ns].tables[i];
-            InitializeCriticalSectionEx( &table->cs, 0, RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION_FLAG_FORCE_DEBUG_INFO );
-            table->cs.DebugInfo->Spare[0] = (DWORD_PTR)(__FILE__ ": table.cs" );
-            list_add_tail( &tables[ns], &table->entry );
+            if (table->flags & TABLE_FLAG_DYNAMIC)
+            {
+                list_remove( &table->entry );
+                release_table( table );
+            }
         }
-        table_list[ns] = &tables[ns];
     }
 }
 
